            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "186. Sick leave shall be applicable only if the employee is ill on days he/she is regularly scheduled to work. If an employee claims sick leave, the Employer may require reasonable proof of physical disability sufficient to justify the employee's absence from work for the period claimed, if the Employer has reasonable doubt of the validity of the disability.",
            "block_bbox": [
                151,
                416,
                1068,
                558
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    151.0,
                    416.0
                ],
                [
                    1068.0,
                    416.0
                ],
                [
                    1068.0,
                    558.0
                ],
                [
                    151.0,
                    558.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "187. An employee hospitalized while on vacation is eligible to convert vacation time to unused sick leave for the period of hospitalization provided reasonable proof of the hospitalization is provided. Conversion of vacation time to sick leave time will apply only to those days the employee was pre-scheduled for vacation",
            "block_bbox": [
                152,
                581,
                1089,
                727
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    152.0,
                    581.0
                ],
                [
                    1089.0,
                    581.0
                ],
                [
                    1089.0,
                    727.0
                ],
                [
                    152.0,
                    727.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "188. An employee who suffers a disabling illness or injury of at least five (5) consecutive days duration while on prescheduled vacation leave, may convert 50% of the verified period of illness to unused sick leave. Such conversion shall be limited to blocks of pre-scheduled vacation of one or more weeks. The employer shall require reasonable proof of the disabling illness or injury, obtained at the time of the disabling event.",
            "block_bbox": [
                151,
                751,
                1090,
                924
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    151.0,
                    751.0
                ],
                [
                    1090.0,
                    751.0
                ],
                [
                    1090.0,
                    924.0
